From: Onyx contributors <onyx@localhost>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:50:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/25] [WTF] RedBlackTree::remove clears the removed node's
 links

The removed node kept its m_left / m_right, CheckedPtrs to its former neighbours: while it lived
on outside the tree, a neighbour could not be deleted without the CheckedPtr crash. The generic
RunLoop keeps its stopped timers' ScheduledTasks alive (each TimerBase owns one), so destroying a
timer whose neighbour in the schedule had been unscheduled earlier crashed -- on Onyx, when the
UI process released a WebProcessProxy or a NetworkProcessProxy (ResponsivenessTimer). insert()
resets a node before linking it, so nothing relied on the stale links.
---
 Source/WTF/wtf/RedBlackTree.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/RedBlackTree.h b/Source/WTF/wtf/RedBlackTree.h
index 3a122a4d..40b9e267 100644
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/RedBlackTree.h
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/RedBlackTree.h
@@ -286,6 +286,12 @@ public:
         } else if (y->color() == Black)
             removeFixup(x, xParent);
 
+        // The removed node keeps no link: its m_left / m_right are CheckedPtrs, and a node they still
+        // pointed to could not be deleted while this one lives on outside the tree (the generic RunLoop's
+        // stopped timers do: a CheckedPtr crash when a neighbour timer was destroyed).
+        z->setLeft(nullptr);
+        z->setRight(nullptr);
+        z->setParent(nullptr);
         return z;
     }
     
